- What's this new util ??
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  LamerKiller is a little util that will stop unwanted users or lamers
  to call !
  It's like EX.BadNames, but only cooler and more crewl :)
  Ex.BadNames only says something like this "You can't use this name!"
  LamerKiller won't be THAT happy. :)
  It will disconnect DIRECTLY, after a nice sequence :)

- What will LAMERKILLER do ??
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  When the user logs in, LamerKiller starts to scan the user,
  if the name is in the datafile of LamerKiller, the user will be
  disconnected! So he/she won't get any further :)))

- How do I install LAMERKILLER ??
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  The datafile & ansifile MUST both be placed in DOORS:LK/
  So just put all files in Doors:LK
  That wouldn't be a problem, because most doors need "doors:" as assign :)
  Add this to your TEXT.WELCOME.USER
  (The best place would be the first line!)
  \#0Doors:LK/Lamer10\

- Files in this archive...
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  * Lamer10         -=> The main file
  * Lamer10.doc     -=> This doc :)
  * Lamer10.dat     -=> The datafile which contains the names of lamers :)
  * Lamer10.ansi    -=> The ansi picture, you must always edit it :^)

- How does this program work ???
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  First it checks if the user is known or not.
  It will say "No" if the user has access 1, if the access is higher
  then 1, it will say "Yes".

  If the user's name is in the datafile, he/she will be disconnected.
  If not, then he/she will enjoy your BBS ! :)

